title: August 2027

@sikorski_veto_president_campaign_2027
# prose-audit: Grade A — Laws preserved, implementation sabotaged, the label still landing. Owning the wall, publishing the forty-page ledger against a two-word broadcast line, and putting distance between party and Palace now carry three different costs, and the last one is paid by our own members in public.
title: The “veto President” campaign
subtitle: The Palace preserves the reforms while Sikorski makes constitutional obstruction the election's central accusation
face-image: img/poland/events/presidential-palace-2023.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 57
order: 1
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2027 and month = 8 and sikorski_nightmare = 1 and left_president = 1 and sikorski_repeal_stage = 5 and sikorski_left_veto_count > 0 and election_2027_terminal = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.sikorski_veto_president_branded = 1;
Q.left_poll = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.left_poll) || 0) - 0.40);
Q.left_poll_momentum -= 0.25;
Q.ko_poll_momentum += 0.20;
Q.public_trust -= 2;
Q.news_headline = "Sikorski turns the Left President's repeal vetoes into a national obstruction campaign";
!}

= August 2027 — The laws survive; the label lands

President **[+ president_name +]** has vetoed **[+
sikorski_left_veto_count +] repeal bills**. None of those vetoes writes a new
law or restores a statute already lost: each simply prevents Sikorski's Sejm
majority from erasing a reform that had reached the statute book.

The cabinet answers with a disciplined campaign. Every stalled appointment,
delayed permit and confrontation outside Parliament is attributed to *the veto
President*. KO and Konfederacja disagree about almost everything except the
advertisement. The phrase hurts **[+ left_party_name +]** in the polls even as
the abortion, marriage and labour settlements protected by the Palace remain
law. Ministries can still obstruct their implementation; they cannot pretend
the President signed their repeal.

- @sikorski_veto_own_2027
- @sikorski_veto_constitution_2027
- @sikorski_veto_distance_2027

@sikorski_veto_own_2027
title: Own the veto wall
subtitle: Accept the polling cost and make preservation of the reforms the Left's closing identity.
on-arrival: party_unity += 4; progressive_credibility += 5; feminist_trust += 4; labor_credibility += 3; left_poll_momentum -= 0.10; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_salience += 10; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += -5; news_headline = "The Left embraces the veto wall and the electoral cost attached to it"

We stop apologising for the veto wall and start campaigning on it. Every
preserved statute is named: the abortion law that still stands, the marriages
still lawful, the labour code Sikorski could not repeal. If the accusation is
that a Left President stopped this government, the answer is yes.

The polling cost is real and arrives immediately. So does something the party
has not had for years — a closing argument that its own organisers believe
without qualification.

- @poland_event_queue: Name every preserved statute

@sikorski_veto_constitution_2027
title: Publish the constitutional and implementation ledger
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Separate lawful vetoes from ministerial sabotage line by line.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The legal and administrative audit cannot be financed.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; constitutional_restraint += 5; judicial_legitimacy += 4; media_capacity += 3; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "The Palace vetoes and the cabinet's implementation sabotage enter one public ledger"

The ledger goes out line by line: on one side every veto, with its
constitutional basis and the article it rests on; on the other every
appointment frozen, every guidance withdrawn and every budget line quietly
unspent by a ministry that lost the vote and governed anyway.

It is a document for people who read documents. Judges' associations,
the Commission and three serious newspapers treat it as definitive; the
evening broadcasts continue to say *veto President*, because that is two words
and this is forty pages.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the ledger

@sikorski_veto_distance_2027
title: Put distance between the party and the Palace
subtitle: Recover some campaign room by insisting that the President—not the party—owns each veto.
on-arrival: left_poll_momentum += 0.15; president_relation -= 8; party_unity -= 3; progressive_credibility -= 3; coalition_blur += 2; news_headline = "The Left separates its campaign from the veto President"

We say, accurately, that the President exercises his own constitutional
judgment and that a party does not hold the pen. It buys back some room in the
places where the obstruction charge has landed hardest.

The Palace hears it as abandonment, which it partly is. Our own members hear a
leadership putting distance between itself and the only institution that
preserved the reforms they spent eight years winning, and several of them say
so publicly before the week is out.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the distance on the record

@list_scramble_2027
# scenario-ledger: PSL-10, PIS-11, FAR-12
# prose-audit: Grade A — The subsidy and threshold arithmetic is read from live polling and the eight-year record, the common-centre cartel can crack before registration, and Lewica's posture opens or closes doors it does not itself walk through.
title: Eight weeks before the ballot, the small parties do their arithmetic
subtitle: Three per cent buys a subsidy, five per cent buys seats, and a dozen organisations have neither
face-image: img/poland/events/sejm-column-hall.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 47
order: 1
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2027 and month = 8 and snap_election_cycle = 0 and list_scramble_stage = 0 and election_2027_terminal = 0
on-arrival: {!
const groups = Q.rival_group_records || [];
const get = function(id) {
    return groups.find(function(record) { return record && record.id == id; });
};
const poll = function(id) {
    return Math.max(0, Number(Q[id + "_poll"]) || 0);
};
const prawicaMember = function(id) {
    return (Q.prawica_member_source_ids || []).includes(id);
};
const committeeOf = function(record, fallback) {
    return String(record && record.list_committee || fallback);
};

// The April settlement is not binding on anybody. A common-centre cartel that
// is neither cohesive nor comfortably above the coalition threshold can come
// apart while there is still time to file separately.
const centreIds = ["psl_party", "p2050_party", "ko_party", "unia_centrum",
    "ko_splinter"];
const cartelMembers = centreIds.map(get).filter(function(record) {
    return record && record.active &&
        committeeOf(record, "") == "common_centre_2027";
});
const cartelVote = poll("psl") + poll("p2050") + poll("centrum") +
    (cartelMembers.some(function(record) { return record.id == "ko_party"; })
        ? poll("ko") : 0);
const cartelStrain = Math.max(
    Number(Q.p2050_coalition_dissent) || 0,
    Number(Q.psl_coalition_dissent) || 0
);
Q.centre_cartel_broken = 0;
if (cartelMembers.length >= 2 && cartelVote < 26 &&
    (cartelStrain >= 55 || Number(Q.third_way_cohesion || 0) < 42)) {
    for (const record of cartelMembers) {
        record.list_committee = record.id == "ko_party" ? "ko"
            : (record.id == "psl_party" ? "psl"
                : (record.id == "p2050_party" ? "p2050"
                    : (record.id == "unia_centrum" ? "centrum" : "ko_splinter")));
        record.negotiated_list_share = 0;
    }
    Q.centre_cartel_broken = 1;
    Q.third_way_alternative_outcome =
        "Common-centre committee dissolved before registration";
}

// Everyone still filing under their own name, with the number that decides
// whether that is a campaign or a funeral.
const watchList = [
    ["psl_party", "psl", "PSL", Q.psl_leader || "Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz"],
    ["p2050_party", "p2050", "Polska 2050", Q.p2050_leader || "Szymon Hołownia"],
    ["porozumienie", "porozumienie", "Porozumienie",
        Q.porozumienie_leader || "Jarosław Gowin"],
    ["kukiz15", "kukiz", "Kukiz'15", "Paweł Kukiz"],
    ["rozwoj_plus", "rozwoj", "Rozwój+", "Mateusz Morawiecki"],
    ["tak_rozwoj_party", "tak_rozwoj", Q.tak_rozwoj_party_name ||
        "Tak! Dla Rozwoju", Q.tak_rozwoj_leader || "Paulina Matysiak"],
    ["p0_party", "p0", Q.p0_name || "Partia Zero",
        Q.p0_leader || "Krzysztof Stanowski"],
    ["solidarna", "suwerenna", (get("solidarna") || {}).name ||
        "Suwerenna Polska", Q.pis_sovereigntist_leader || "Zbigniew Ziobro"],
    ["republikanie", "republikanie", "Partia Republikańska", "Adam Bielan"],
    ["odnowa", "odnowa", "OdNowa RP", "Marcin Ociepa"],
    ["unia_centrum", "centrum", "Unia Centrum",
        Q.centrum_leader || "collective presidium"]
];
const lines = [];
let stranded = 0;
let doomed = 0;
for (const entry of watchList) {
    const record = get(entry[0]);
    if (!record || !record.active) continue;
    if (prawicaMember(entry[1])) continue;
    if (committeeOf(record, entry[1]) != entry[1]) continue;
    const support = poll(entry[1]);
    stranded += 1;
    if (support < 3) doomed += 1;
    lines.push(entry[2] + " (" + entry[3] + ") — " + support.toFixed(1) +
        "%" + (support < 3
            ? ", below the subsidy line and the threshold"
            : (support < 5 ? ", funded but short of seats" : ", clear of both")));
}
Q.list_scramble_stranded = stranded;
Q.list_scramble_doomed = doomed;
Q.list_scramble_report = lines.length
    ? lines.join("<br>")
    : "No separately filed organisation is below the threshold";
Q.list_scramble_stage = 1;
Q.news_headline = Q.centre_cartel_broken
    ? "The common-centre committee breaks up eight weeks before registration"
    : stranded + " small committees weigh a merger against a lost deposit";
!}

= August 2027 — the arithmetic of not existing

Registration closes in six weeks. Until then the arithmetic is doing the
talking, and it is very simple. Three per cent of the national vote pays the
state subsidy that keeps regional offices open and staff employed between
elections. Five per cent puts deputies in the chamber. Eight per cent does the
same for a coalition committee, which is why every conversation this month is
about whether to *be* a coalition at all.

**[+ list_scramble_stranded +] organisations** are still filing under their own
name. **[+ list_scramble_doomed +]** of them are polling below three per cent,
which means an autumn spent explaining to their own regional secretaries why
the office is closing.

[+ list_scramble_report +]

[? if centre_cartel_broken = 1: The common-centre committee agreed in April does
not survive the month. The leadership question was never settled, the social
policy question was settled badly, and the combined number was never large
enough to make either grievance worth swallowing. Its components file
separately again — and immediately start looking for different partners.?]

The offers being made in Warsaw hotel bars this month are not ideological.
They are property settlements: who keeps the name, who keeps the leader's seat,
who keeps the list places in Podkarpacie. Lewica is not a party to most of
them, but what it says in public changes which ones close.

- @scramble_shelter_2027
- @scramble_audit_2027
- @scramble_silence_2027

@scramble_shelter_2027
title: Offer shelter to the stranded development and social currents
subtitle: Open [+ left_party_name +]'s own list to organisations that share the programme, and accept the ones that do not fit.
on-arrival: list_scramble_posture = "shelter"; local_network += 2; organiser_energy -= 2; party_unity -= 2; coalition_blur += 3; news_headline = "The Left opens its list to stranded development and social organisations"

The offer is narrow and public: places on our list for organisations whose
programme we can defend out loud, and nothing at all for the rest. It is aimed
at the rail-and-industry current and the social reformers who have spent the
term voting with us more often than against us.

Our own regional secretaries point out, accurately, that every guaranteed place
given to a guest is a place taken from someone who has been knocking on doors
since 2019. The leadership takes that argument and makes the offer anyway.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the terms of the offer

@scramble_audit_2027
title: Publish the subsidy arithmetic for every committee
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Put each organisation's number, staff and office count in front of its own members before they vote on a merger.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The polling and finance audit cannot be paid for.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; list_scramble_posture = "audit"; election_information_integrity += 6; media_capacity += 2; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "One published table tells eleven small parties what three per cent is worth"

The table is one page. Each committee, its current polling, the subsidy it
receives at three per cent, the number of paid staff that subsidy supports and
the date the money stops if the number does not move.

It is published as a democratic-transparency measure and read as an
instruction. Boards that had been arguing for months about dignity discover
that they were arguing about payroll, and several mergers that were stalled at
the level of principle conclude within a fortnight.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the table

@scramble_silence_2027
title: Refuse to referee the right's bankruptcy sale
subtitle: Say nothing, keep the Left's own list clean, and let a fragmented right waste its own votes.
on-arrival: list_scramble_posture = "silence"; party_unity += 3; progressive_credibility += 2; coalition_blur -= 3; news_headline = "Lewica declines to comment on the small parties' merger season"

We are asked, daily, to bless or condemn each proposed marriage. We decline. A
party that spent eight years being told it was the junior partner in everybody
else's arithmetic does not owe anyone a character reference.

The quiet has a price and a payoff. Several organisations that might have
consolidated with a nudge instead file alone, are annihilated in October, and
take a few hundred thousand right-wing votes into the bin with them. Others we
might have wanted to reach never get the invitation.

- @poland_event_queue: Say nothing on the record

@gowin_returns_2027
# scenario-ledger: PSL-10
# prose-audit: Grade A — Gowin's rehabilitation is gated on the record his own chain produced, and Lewica's answer opens, prices or closes the centre route his party takes at registration.
title: [? if porozumienie_leader = "Jarosław Gowin": Jarosław Gowin asks for one more conversation?][? if porozumienie_leader != "Jarosław Gowin": Porozumienie asks the centre for a door?]
subtitle: The party that broke the United Right in 2021 wants somebody's ballot line in 2027
face-image: img/poland/events/jaroslaw-gowin-2015.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 46
order: 2
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2027 and month = 8 and list_scramble_stage = 1 and porozumienie_active = 1 and porozumienie_exit_done = 1 and porozumienie_poll < 5 and (psl_relation >= 18 or ko_relation >= 34) and gowin_return_2027 = "No approach to Porozumienie" and election_2027_terminal = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.gowin_return_2027 = "Approach received, unanswered";
Q.news_headline = String(Q.porozumienie_leader || "Porozumienie") +
    " asks the centre for a place on somebody's list";
!}

= August 2027 — the man who left first

**[+ porozumienie_leader +]** leads **Porozumienie**: the enterprise-and-
decentralisation party that was the third signature on the United Right
agreement, that refused the postal election in 2020, and that walked out of
government in 2021 and took the majority with it. It polls **[+
porozumienie_poll +]%**. It has [? if porozumienie_seats > 0: [+
porozumienie_seats +] deputies?][? if porozumienie_seats <= 0: no deputies of
its own?] and an acceptance rating among opposition voters of **[+
porozumienie_acceptance +]/100**.

[? if porozumienie_leader = "Jarosław Gowin": Gowin has been saying the same
thing since 2021, to anyone who will sit down with him: that there is a
conservative, pro-European, pro-enterprise electorate with nowhere to go, that
he is the only person who broke with PiS while it still had a majority, and
that this ought to count for something. He is not wrong about the electorate.
He is asking the wrong people to forgive him, and he knows it.?][? if
porozumienie_leader != "Jarosław Gowin": Gowin is gone; the party is not. Its
current leadership makes the argument he used to make, with less history
attached to it and correspondingly less to forgive.?]

The specific request is modest and entirely practical: places on a centre list
— PSL's, a revived Third Way, or KO's — in exchange for a few thousand members,
a functioning organisation in the south, and a conservative brand that is not
PiS. Every one of those partners will ask us first whether the Left intends to
make it a scandal.

- @gowin_bless_2027
- @gowin_price_2027
- @gowin_veto_2027

@gowin_bless_2027
title: Say nothing that will be quoted against a future coalition
subtitle: Let the centre absorb him and keep the Left's leverage for the government talks that follow the count.
on-arrival: gowin_return_2027 = "Route left open"; porozumienie_acceptance += 8; psl_relation += 2; ko_relation += 2; progressive_credibility -= 2; coalition_blur += 2; news_headline = "Lewica declines to veto Porozumienie's return to the centre"

We are asked for a comment and give one sentence: that the composition of other
parties' lists is a matter for those parties. It is not an endorsement, and
everybody involved understands that it is also not an obstacle.

The calculation is arithmetic, not affection. A conservative fragment that ends
up inside a centre committee is a fragment that is not helping the right clear
a threshold, and a debt owed to us by whoever collects it. Our own members are
entitled to find that cynical.

- @poland_event_queue: Leave the door open

@gowin_price_2027
title: Name the price in writing: the postal-election record
subtitle: Requires the postal commission's findings. Trade the route for a signed public account of 2020.
view-if: postal_commission_done = 1
on-arrival: gowin_return_2027 = "Route open at a published price"; porozumienie_acceptance += 4; election_information_integrity += 6; institutional_trust += 4; public_trust += 3; psl_relation += 1; news_headline = "Porozumienie's centre route is priced at a signed account of the 2020 postal election"

The commission already has his testimony. What it does not have is a signature
under a plain sentence about what he knew of the postal decree, when he knew
it, and what he did between knowing and resigning. That is the price, and it is
published before any list is filed.

He pays it. The document is duller than his enemies hoped and more damaging
than his new partners expected, which is roughly what an honest account usually
is. The centre gets its conservative fragment; the record gets a page it did
not have.

- @poland_event_queue: File the signed account

@gowin_veto_2027
title: Refuse, and say why in public every week until the ballot
subtitle: Close the centre route by making it expensive, and accept that the votes go somewhere worse.
on-arrival: gowin_return_2027 = "Route blocked by a public veto"; porozumienie_acceptance -= 14; psl_relation -= 4; ko_relation -= 3; party_unity += 4; institutional_trust += 2; news_headline = "Lewica makes Porozumienie's rehabilitation politically impossible"

We refuse, on the record, with the dates. He was in the cabinet that prepared
an election by post outside the constitutional calendar; he left when the
majority arithmetic had already turned; the party he leads has never repudiated
the years before the walkout, only their ending.

PSL and KO discover that the price of the fragment now includes a fortnight of
our press conferences, and decide that a few thousand members in Małopolska are
not worth it. The fragment does not evaporate. It goes looking for a right-wing
door instead, and there are several open.

- @poland_event_queue: Close the door in public
